#: bef01dcc7218433c966ad5de1e12bd80 c61e994ed1d748f784c470e47dc5be25
#: dc27bb113af64ff497b2d26270a48881 e2dbadad6768480b96052c2de8da96e6
#: e89d8788992543098f5f5db2e742e9aa e8b4870d1994482bae4965aa14bf88dc
msgid "Cable Recommendations"
msgstr "线缆建议"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:45
#: 0fe5421013f6417ab4a3e86f022abd2b 14763ac23a7946ca9d9f0f24b859acc1
#: 5de90de90129497ebd99a7fd9fde5586 7616798d805447f4b45bdb1648920929
#: 988624b3ee33491cae037859feb71f06
msgid ""
"Proper cable handling is mandatory for reliable I2C communication, as "
"inappropriately routed I2C signals could be prone to electromagnetic "
"interference (EMI) and crosstalk."
msgstr "可靠的I2C通信必须正确处理线缆，因为布线不当的I2C信号容易受到电磁干扰（EMI）和串扰的影响。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:47
#: 0dd5fad16e364c87952920b169876380 2bef24b7a18b4276aa9fd523cdb5f438
#: 3c731e8e70784199a1f1924a9c5d0519 57fbadd853ad4ad7bb68831ba4cbd0c1
#: 7c0cc8de8a8e4812a1a788a2758330f5
msgid "Keep cables as short as possible."
msgstr "线缆尽量短。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:48
#: 224002a577874466a7794f87af2b0e45 618d88dbc73c4155a951425dd867ce6c
#: bfa8746be21a4e76b483b77d75b5ed29 dd39fe94911c43f9a6dd7b18a74efe36
#: f48fa5a532e34c52b9e630ac517ae824
msgid ""
"Use twisted pairs to reduce crosstalk: - Twist each pair (SCL/+5V and "
"SDA/GND) about 10 turns per 30 cm. - Twist both pairs together about 4 turns"
" per 30 cm."
msgstr "使用双绞线减少串扰：- 每对（SCL/+5V和SDA/GND）每30cm约绞合10圈。- 两对合并每30cm约绞合4圈。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:51
#: 11f263272265447ca82c840fa0f47197 2a6556b4a81649ec8c87ba5e4a6762cd
#: 65eaf8067ade4db2ae79ee581d3c431d 832d6d710e71488fbb1b52eeb28acde3
#: f12d1d6915f64dc79027dc9699601ce6
msgid ""
"For larger vehicles or long cables, consider using CAN bus or other "
"differential signaling interfaces instead."
msgstr "对于较大的飞行器或较长的线缆，建议使用CAN总线或其他差分信号接口代替。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:54
#: 4050cba1128f4af7b5cba716b7f96485 5b35db437e894061987271048f5c24cd
#: 7512e29e9f154bf58f751e008af9c219 8418aba95ae7466abb0f175937b154f1
#: ea488926f54448c0ba081ef2d2fc79ce
msgid "Pull-up Resistors"
msgstr "上拉电阻"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:55
#: 70007dd8bec0487f8be3147931c91cd5 7c0bc8d6a54646519a8ae6141fca7c92
#: 7e44088d59b3420daee99a8082b2c2aa c5912ec9093a428a82309fe9069b6481
#: ce78311089d24e95922a18e1b4111ccf
msgid ""
"Pull-up resistors on both SDA and SCL lines are essential. Autopilots or "
"peripheral devices typically have these resistors built-in. An oscilloscope "
"measurement is sometimes required to check correct value of pull-up "
"resistors. If the signal amplitude is too low, increase resistor values. If "
"the signals are rounded, decrease resistor values."
msgstr ""
"SDA和SCL线上的上拉电阻必不可少。飞控或外围设备通常内置这些电阻。有时需要用示波器检查上拉电阻值是否正确。若信号幅度太低，增大电阻值；若信号出现圆滑，减小电阻值。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:58
#: 27a025d52349457bbbdbcda044d9b383 5378a5e4889b41e5a0763a8680ec8230
#: 696ed771015c40629db5b36e469ecc09 967630cd4faa480697db38019229eddc
#: ddd1fc43602d4bf2a871274cab0c2df2
msgid "Common Problems"
msgstr "常见问题"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:59
#: 0a254783040247118b8ce02b04121036 26c38d6d2ab140d0a55508207789331f
#: 812f3aeb02034965a80b7e0980c2cf65 84f10232fa9d4822964a8a111701dadf
#: cf09f8c04fa744ba844868159c09e0a0
msgid ""
"**Address Clashes**: Occur when multiple devices on the bus share the same "
"address, preventing proper communication. Possible solutions include: - "
"Changing the device's address via hardware or software configuration, if "
"supported. - Use an address translator to remap address, such as from "
"`ThunderFly <https://docs.thunderfly.cz/avionics/TFI2CADT01/>`__ or "
"`Adafruit <https://www.adafruit.com/product/5914>`__."
msgstr ""
"**地址冲突**：当总线上多个设备共享同一地址时发生，导致通信异常。可能的解决方案包括：- 通过硬件或软件配置更改设备地址（如支持）。- "
"使用地址转换器重新映射地址，例如来自 `ThunderFly "
"<https://docs.thunderfly.cz/avionics/TFI2CADT01/>`__ 或 `Adafruit "
"<https://www.adafruit.com/product/5914>`__ 的产品。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:63
#: 487748530ebc403aa5a6af56667ae25b 57dcd316b077411da24dc2db4d016996
#: 93a16abdfe974c669824fded31bfd8d5 c60c6fb5637e4579974287c7c88c223c
#: c87aef5b9d7a4af79aa8542bd58cabf9
msgid ""
"**Excessive Wiring Capacitance**: Long cables or multiple devices connected "
"to a single bus significantly increase cable capacitance, resulting in "
"degraded signal quality. Possible solutions include:"
msgstr "**线缆电容过大**：较长线缆或连接至同一总线的多个设备会显著增加线缆电容，导致信号质量下降。可能的解决方案包括："

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:65
#: 492b630b1ad2462d8725d34f70c0c9a9 9826836fdebb457bab86de4844f4b6ad
#: cf23d42486414dafa5f292fd8823e35b e489954bf4334cf98322d30b69f82ad0
#: e6793cbbfe644f92be761c1f7e5c0e8a
msgid "Reducing cable length or using higher-quality cables."
msgstr "缩短线缆长度或使用更高质量的线缆。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:66
#: 47feb0a9575849029347d2d797521bef 59d4ea2c75a048029c6dbb711b1063e6
#: ae0dd0d0ed9143078fc58548b6075d00 c8ea569c22c142ef88d3a030e45eb363
#: e6f22f0558ad49858ab6c99fd3c94347
msgid "Splitting devices across multiple I2C buses."
msgstr "将设备分布在多条I2C总线上。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:67
#: 134b72af2ba34ccb838e0f65fbcb0868 3546044783fd4f0aa882a3e5c0958ab9
#: 8cbb82d778104c37abd8a77da0577bbb 9f53f85efc114d8aad21f14d65cbdfa1
#: bad16991077e425fb652d4cb7dae2fe7
msgid ""
"Use an I2C bus extender such as `Adafruit I2C Extender "
"<https://www.adafruit.com/product/4756>`__ , or `ThundeFly's I2C bus "
"accelerators or extenders "
"<https://docs.thunderfly.cz/avionics/TFI2CEXT01/>`__ to boost signal quality"
" over extended cable lengths."
msgstr ""
"使用I2C总线扩展器，如 `Adafruit I2C扩展器 <https://www.adafruit.com/product/4756>`__ 或 "
"`ThunderFly的I2C总线加速器/扩展器 "
"<https://docs.thunderfly.cz/avionics/TFI2CEXT01/>`__，以在较长线缆上提升信号质量。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:70
#: 006f09d0adfd47ebbd67b6426cde8f0c 07caf31c81094efb96e6b6d472d9fa1f
#: 84aea029ce4b4c2eaaa4dab62684a3d7 8a9577d3e83546af94cd4f1d87107160
#: c13319a97da24ffc9ad54f3ce95e19a0
msgid "CAN"
msgstr "CAN"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:71
#: 03c72a15c56b4b44b1d2e72fdc8c7b41 04e032c737f14ef9b2a2376b2540b8b9
#: 502c0955acc745f9ad7b7bfdf945f549 9aa459115fea4ce7bc23f72cbe2d3a7f
#: ce53e0e8d2bc4a5c9a9a6d3283c4c8f4
msgid ""
":ref:`CAN <common-canbus-setup-advanced>` bus is provided on many autopilots"
" for use with :ref:`DroneCAN <common-uavcan-setup-advanced>` peripherals. "
"ESCs, GPS/Compass, Rangefinders, and many other peripherals and sensors are "
"being added to the list of available DroneCAN devices everyday. CAN provides"
" a robust method of communicating with peripherals with data integrity, even"
" with long leads."
msgstr ""
":ref:`CAN <common-canbus-setup-advanced>` 总线在许多飞控上提供，用于连接 :ref:`DroneCAN "
"<common-uavcan-setup-advanced>` "
"外设。ESC、GPS/罗盘、测距仪及许多其他外设和传感器正不断加入可用DroneCAN设备列表。CAN即使在较长引线下也能提供具有数据完整性的可靠外设通信方法。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:76
#: 2498cb6ed01142dfbf7277ef2ffe96d8 36798cb931d3401db510abfd546ae4df
#: 9598e968a3f54879abac62e1fed43dcc 9af4010ec02d4aea9c1b7d9c5b48b429
#: c2e20f07d88245d99ff1c84ca49c0bf2
msgid ""
"CAN cables should use twisted pairs to reduce electromagnetic interference "
"(EMI) and maintain signal integrity on cables over 6 inches:"
msgstr "超过6英寸的CAN线缆应使用双绞线以减少电磁干扰（EMI）并保持信号完整性："

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:78
#: 2a2e1d679f324b9891584595bf089e60 2e5e4026597f4b56ade652c2da76ee61
#: 33057245b06e444291abffec10204eb4 4ebd3827281e46e4885172efdb2b86ab
#: 78dfc5c94192476883f6a41067d3a648
msgid ""
"Twist each signal pair (CAN_H/CAN_L and +5V/GND) approximately 10 turns per "
"30 cm."
msgstr "每对信号线（CAN_H/CAN_L和+5V/GND）每30cm约绞合10圈。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:79
#: 716fb64f7b8e464394192f716175ca4b 8d53d9d5e9284c1dae6d6891338e1b38
#: 9050ad97c7154ed2809ee9e310922383 a85f0c5bbc9d4e798f9a676966401886
#: f08777d2b9194c9687474a8d0e9c4209
msgid "Twist both pairs together about 4 turns per 30 cm."
msgstr "两对合并每30cm约绞合4圈。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:80
#: 046d5cd4c6f34f36810c442471095ec2 16971909636c4cdfac9fef06772c394e
#: 35107cd9c0b64af8928c7ddcde4b83cc 97c1a9bee0cd4d3d846fa0e095905a26
#: c9b094af024940f1a8efd2b054645f75
msgid "Maintain separation from high-power and high-noise cables."
msgstr "与高功率和高噪声线缆保持距离。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:82
#: 16381459fdfd47898a0d590d78c76ed0 455ec5cf32a04bd7be45818c53c08f03
#: 646f5280b5344510a864388c6c4d0c07 7d256073afb64348b1d6c5d1688cd28b
#: d5a7bbd871164a8b9dacc664ee3f3675
msgid ""
"Due to its differential signaling and robust protocol, CAN is particularly "
"suitable for applications requiring reliability over longer cable lengths "
"and in electrically noisy environments."
msgstr "由于其差分信号和健壮协议，CAN特别适用于对较长线缆和电气噪声环境中的可靠性有要求的应用场景。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:85
#: 44e121c1605a4a7e91042f206224f56a 8023f7fa55d84a76b50474a1fdcc760b
#: 96541e74b7764650ad67fcc203fe9d02 c0a128863e104b5e8ee057da291b6de9
#: c55231262d804cb5882b179bfb60efba
msgid "SPI"
msgstr "SPI"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:86
#: 0d99e7086c7340399e9962cc8e554dfa 33b8f054b6ac4c4390ede985f3647eed
#: 501b9a7488464629ab6ee53ae0cf8940 53096f124bdf4997ac0b3881ff7a4807
#: 585135868eeb4fd7b3a5ce6234720e93
msgid ""
"SPI (Serial Peripheral Interface) is a synchronous serial communication "
"protocol used by autopilots to connect higher-bandwidth peripherals and "
"sensors, such as optical flow sensors, specialized telemetry modems, "
"barometers, IMUs, and other advanced digital sensors. It supports full-"
"duplex communication using separate lines for data input and output. Most "
"autopilots have processors with multiple SPI ports."
msgstr ""
"SPI（串行外设接口）是飞控用于连接较高带宽外设和传感器的同步串行通信协议，如光流传感器、专用数传调制解调器、气压计、IMU和其他先进数字传感器。它支持使用独立数据输入和输出线的全双工通信。大多数飞控处理器具有多个SPI接口。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:90
#: 1f62af43ce5b4022a9126d4cd4bd7575 6562a41c255f4a3fba45673d0954af9e
#: b78e710fcc1b4b7eb11937f574380b5a cc71fb80d522479aa450c17e6e599533
#: dae74b0cb83845c180892aaad14d1e05
msgid ""
"SPI signals can be sensitive to electromagnetic interference (EMI) and "
"crosstalk, especially at higher clock rates. To minimize these issues:"
msgstr "SPI信号可能对电磁干扰（EMI）和串扰敏感，尤其是在较高时钟频率下。为减少这些问题："

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:92
#: 02a1e71273aa45c180ba331bc253fc66 3690278efcf442c8b8bb9ff2dd84d816
#: b75b9694f20d4cc18769b3aac24d0a0b bf4b48db76034097a63160b9f43a9933
#: e366b116aa9a4369ba7463b7bb87de5b
msgid "Keep cable lengths as short as possible."
msgstr "线缆长度尽量短。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:93
#: 0e6218c1ba0d4b729d53b9103cabdaa6 27680d77a51d4dc0be3ac104fe646a42
#: 4649792f0c6d4491b8ba28067963e214 7555ccbfaf6348cd81c2824d84925eb9
#: 75f6020999214bb98fc91536572a382a
msgid "Ensure signal cables are separated from high-power and noisy cables."
msgstr "确保信号线缆与高功率和噪声线缆分开。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:96
#: 0692c3bfb9904e0c8a331e04cdd82d74 7091d90452824cbba81afc40e8a9bbbc
#: 8daa272ae9bb4f5395251f7e391815d8 a9e3fcdc41e1452fb9457aa4588a0bcf
#: f44d748c6a314832843d99e694e7cdd7
msgid "UART"
msgstr "UART"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:97
#: 4f4529788238402f9254d8f6f79d5c67 a8f84952a5fe405aaab00eb75579a3ff
#: bd33c2e570af45f092d174f37fb7b729 c893148bf60b4298b9283330d7bb62d7
#: fc0f26ab09aa456ca297e57a48869316
msgid ""
"UART (Universal Asynchronous Receiver/Transmitter) ports are commonly "
"provided by autopilots to connect peripherals such as telemetry radios, GPS "
"receivers, rangefinders, radio modems, and even SBUS servos. Serial RC "
"receiver inputs can be connected to any UART. See :ref:`Serial Port "
"Configuration <common-serial-options>`. Usually, several UART ports are "
"provided."
msgstr ""
"UART（通用异步收发器）接口常见于飞控，用于连接数传电台、GPS接收机、测距仪、无线调制解调器乃至SBUS舵机等外设。串行RC接收机输入可连接至任意UART。参见"
" :ref:`串口配置 <common-serial-options>`。通常提供多个UART接口。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:99
#: 1bce46577dff45259246911b0c475e39 3f6e04c8024742adb45e497bea1ddde7
#: 7c76f0ef0cc94b988106e87c6c182fe5 d929a53f76204557939a2b0e426c0540
#: fef9cadc50024f42810af6760311b2e6
msgid ""
"By default, UART connections are point-to-point and do not support bus-style"
" networking. Each UART line directly connects two devices. The connecting "
"cable is typically straight (1:1), meaning no crossing is performed within "
"the cable itself. Therefore, the peripheral devices must internally cross "
"RX/TX signals as required."
msgstr ""
"默认情况下，UART连接为点对点，不支持总线型网络。每条UART线路直接连接两台设备。连接线缆通常为直连（1:1），即线缆内部不进行交叉。因此，外围设备必须在内部按需交叉RX/TX信号。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:101
#: 2739ac42ace04cd5aab8b27c089f9bf2 2bac6fb7b85546219f0df9c6bee6bb09
#: 5a25a41d4b474e1d959e26bc9a7f84dc 696fcf08c6b74314bacb99acda9c0562
#: a6331ab365304787be9621c6632ca706
msgid ""
"Some UART ports provide CTS (Clear To Send) and RTS (Request To Send) "
"signals to allow  a hardware handshake mechanism that improves reliability "
"by preventing data overflow. If the peripheral does not utilize these "
"signals, they can typically remain disconnected. ArduPilot also provides a "
"means to disable this flow control using the ``BRD_SERx_RTSCTS`` parameters."
msgstr ""
"部分UART接口提供CTS（清除发送）和RTS（请求发送）信号，通过硬件握手机制提高可靠性，防止数据溢出。若外围设备不使用这些信号，通常可保持断开。ArduPilot也提供了通过"
" ``BRD_SERx_RTSCTS`` 参数禁用流控制的方法。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:105
#: 78977a01b6cc49e3a34ca938b9f7b8d0 7ef604e92df640b481c167ad818912f0
#: 8f00fc5c4f3a4496babb6e54e76658dc c0f8950cfe634b81835476afe588cc98
#: dcf7fe1ae62c42f2836b7d822a2a12ce
msgid ""
"UART signals, particularly at higher baud rates, can generate "
"electromagnetic interference (EMI). However, this is not normally an issue "
"in most vehicles. However, to minimize EMI:"
msgstr "UART信号，尤其是在较高波特率下，可能产生电磁干扰（EMI）。但在大多数飞行器中通常不是问题。为减少EMI："

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:107
#: 29afd98eceb94ec98948f1c56bd005e7 41b24502e0be40ffb0c2739cb0e996c9
#: 88174a264bbe4abaad5f122f31d19dff 93dab0977e3c4dd999afd46004f6f330
#: ce2b6a4545e64657a2a72b35ac9e8d7b
msgid "Keep UART cable lengths as short as practical."
msgstr "UART线缆长度尽量短。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:108
#: 41c66c3d644d4811b18849a6e09433b8 5263f7b42cc441c68bab84d5cb6c94ec
#: 7f19f1c1bd8640b2b2a0ac93763a3d91 bd2005aed1474f0abc38bac7ca8e1f3c
#: f184305dd6a24093b9087ebcb939a4da
msgid ""
"Separate UART cables from high-power wires and sensitive sensors, such as "
"GPS receivers and magnetometers."
msgstr "将UART线缆与高功率导线和敏感传感器（如GPS接收机和磁力计）分开。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-cabling-guide.rst:110
#: 30bc807d42de4fd0875d0dda92cf34b7 3c4dc40977954b9da77595552ae3f5f4
#: 56407402eb3e4a768a97edc883ba9ecc 992f6f9d905647afbaf9493ad1ec9b1b
#: b456d873039b4ca899a197ce3e32aa9d
msgid ""
"Unlike twisted-pair cables used for differential protocols (CAN, I2C), cable"
" twisting is generally not applicable for UART signals due to their single-"
"ended nature."
msgstr "与差分协议（CAN、I2C）使用的双绞线不同，由于UART信号的单端特性，线缆绞合通常不适用于UART信号。"
